"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T20:29:15-08:00","id":7161,"title":"","content":"Well given that the 11th's run is ending at the end of this year, the Ponds are the significant companions of the 11th Doctor just by being the only other ones in his entire run. Not that they don't deserve it, their story has been just as interesting as the Doctor's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T01:17:18-08:00","id":10257,"title":"","content":"I've been watching Sleepy Hollow and Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. Well, that and Korra now that the new season is underway (and the new season of MLP should be starting soon