liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:11:00-08:00","id":13570,"title":"","content":"Coven is so good. Going to be taking some inspiration for it for my next WoD mortals game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T16:32:11-08:00","id":13685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=13380#post13380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm watching Chuck (finally), Continuum (great show) and Dexter (again, finally) right now. Just got done with Fringe, loved it. Watched Ripper Street series 1 recently, and it was quite well done. Netflix is sooooo wrth $8 a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite enjoyed Continuum. I'm all caught up on Netflix, though, so waiting time for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:12:13-08:00","id":14055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=10276#post10276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished watching all the episodes of The Originals, it's better than I thought it would be. Planning on checking out Dracula next, but I've heard bad things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been enjoying The Originals as well. I've been finding Dracula to be a bit underwhelming myself. I had high hopes for it, but so far they haven't been met. Something about the actress playing Mina bothers me. I didn't care for her as The Huntress on Arrow either. Speaking of, I've also been watching Arrow. I'm liking the second season more than the first. They're dipping their toes into the greater DC universe quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T12:08:58-08:00","id":14212,"title":"","content":"Still watching Supernatural, appreciating the pace they're taking with Arrow development, and just started watching Almost Human, though I've been anticipating that one for awhile now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T16:04:09-08:00","id":14345,"title":"","content":"The Originals has made me happy for three reasons. I enjoy the world of <i>TVD</i>, so a spinoff show is a plus. <i>TVD</i> was starting to suffer from a &quot;supernatural arms race&quot; where each season they introduced a new, bigger, badder supernatural threat. The really good stories were drowning under the sheer delirium of being constantly threatened by some insane new threat. <i>The Originals</i> has provided for a location to shunt off most of those insane threats (New Orleans) while giving them room to further develop those stories. This split has provided the space the enlarging cast of characters needed to grow.<br /> <br /> I watched the first two episodes of <i>Almost Human</i> last night and I am very happy with it. There is a lot of great chemistry in the cast and they are building a very complex, rich setting to explore.<br /> <br /> I love everything about <i>Sleepy Hollow</i> except actress Nicole Beharie. She bugs me, the actress. Not the character. Tom Mison is a phenomenal Ichabod Crane, and the rest of the cast and show are top notch, imho.<br /> <br /> @Dem - I agree. Dracula has been underwhelming so far. I did read one article by an advance viewer who says the show picks up after the fifth episode. For that reason, I have been hanging in there and hoping what I read is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T16:13:15-08:00","id":14351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=14345#post14345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Dem - I agree. Dracula has been underwhelming so far. I did read one article by an advance viewer who says the show picks up after the fifth episode. For that reason, I have been hanging in there and hoping what I read is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, maybe I'll keep watching to see if it does pick up then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T16:35:55-08:00","id":14361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me too... though the recent episode &quot;Dog Dean Afternoon&quot; very nearly made me stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already believe that is the episode we are just going to pretend didn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T18:11:46-08:00","id":14417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\