.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T08:15:55-08:00","id":19189,"title":"","content":"I am starting to love The Originals. Last episode Klaus was a gods damn beast! (Yet the whole time I'm thinking of the B&amp;S rules for BP+frenzy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T19:35:07-08:00","id":21406,"title":"","content":"The mid-season finale of the Walking Dead was heartbreakingly great. I can't wait for it to return next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T19:39:14-08:00","id":22828,"title":"","content":"I'm watching Supernatural, Arrow, Agents of Shield, Walking Dead, and Homeland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1485-robwolf","name":"RobWolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1485_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T23:46:26-08:00","id":52189,"title":"","content":"My mother - who, despite not fitting the stereotypes, is far nerdier than she will admit - stumbled across <i>Lost Girl</i>, and shared the first episode with me this evening.<br /> <br /> I may or may not watch more of it. Like any SyFy show, it sets up an interesting world to explore but gets a bit cheesy sometimes. It was also a bit disorienting, because for the first two-thirds of the episode, I was thinking Kenzi was the main &quot;viewpoint&quot; character rather than Bo. Even after I worked out that Bo was the series' primary protagonist, I kinda found Kenzi's antics to be the more interesting part of their partnership. Any input on the series' quality?<br /> <br /> (Also, just a sidenote: if two groups are trying to recruit you, and they call themselves Light and Dark, who in their right mind is going to choose Dark? Has that label ever <i>not </i>equated to evil? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:10:31-08:00","id":52210,"title":"","content":"Never seen the show, but I'd go with Dark. Then again my heroes growing up were Megatron, Cobra Commander, and Mum-ra. Right now I'm happy Being Human is back on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T05:24:36-08:00","id":52306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=52189#post52189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any input on the series's quality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. I only watched a handful of episodes during the first season, so maybe things have changed since then, but I wasn't impressed. The show wanted to be <b>Buffy the Vampire Slayer</b> so badly it wept itself to sleep every night after posting slashfic of Buffy and Willow online, and I just wasn't interested. To be fair, though, I wasn't prepared to to forgive the show for the laziness of making good fae and evil fae instead of fae who were just goddamned people with different views and agendas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T05:50:42-08:00","id":52315,"title":"","content":"Okay, who cluttered up my desk? Can't find the Netflix info so I can catch up on Doctor Who and several movies (it's Elisabeth's account that we all share). I hate to wake her up just so I can get my David Tennant fix.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah...Sherlock comes on PBS tomorrow night at 9 CST...right after Revenge, Mom's show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:44:43-08:00","id":52494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=52306#post52306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. I only watched a handful of episodes during the first season, so maybe things have changed since then, but I wasn't impressed. The show wanted to be <b>Buffy the Vampire Slayer</b> so badly it wept itself to sleep every night after posting slashfic of Buffy and Willow online, and I just wasn't interested. To be fair, though, I wasn't prepared to to forgive the show for the laziness of making good fae and evil fae instead of fae who were just goddamned people with different views and agendas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is one of those shows I still DVR, but I feel no rush to watch each episode. Usually I watch it when I have finally exhausted all the other shows I really want to watch, then I kill time catching up with Lost Girl. It gets a tiny bit better, but not much. Then again, it doesn't get any worse either.<br /> <br /> Dracula has picked up. A while back I mentioned an advance critic promised the show would pick up eventually, and he was not wrong. Heading into the season finale, the show is doing really well. For having such a slow start, I am going to miss this one until next season. I hope it gets renewed. However, even if it doesn't, it looks like they are ending the season at a place that could also be the series finale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:27:14-08:00","id":52910,"title":"","content":"Currently watching Arrow, Supernatural and Sons of Anarchy. They are all decent. Is it just me or do all tv series look more or less the same nowadays? They are all serial dramas and they are written and filmed in the same manner. Very plot heavy with lots of plot twists. I mean I just watched a superhero, an urban fantasy and a crime show and they are all interchangeable.<br /> <br /> Oh I also took the time to finally watch the Wire. It was an my list for ages and I never wanted to watch it, because I was afraid of a socially engaged heavy drama series. And that is exactly what it is, but I enjoyed the hell out of it. Sometimes very slow and nothing happened, but in the end it pays off because the characters are very three dimensional. In a way just like Breaking Bad.<br /> <br /> Is that American Horror flick really good? It looked kinda cheesy from the trailers.<br /> And the Immortals? Really? Is that better than the Vampire Diaries? Or is it more supernatural romance?<br /> <br /> Oh next on the list is House of Cards. Supposed to be really good.<br /> <br /> And I should give the Walking Dead a second chance. I didn't like the early episodes of the first season with the main character acting like a tool all the time. Never watched it again, but I heard it gets better with time.<br /> <br /> And I try to avoid Agents of Shield, Falling Skies, Revolution etc. Too middle of the road for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 01-18-2014, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://fo