e and Elijah is crushing on the girl Klaus knocked up. That's it for romance so far. Other than that it's been very Requiem, dominating people to use as spies and dealing with mortals. It started slow (they felt the need to introduce everyone) but the last couple of episodes were ace. I recommend trying it out at least. <i>and it has Rebekah</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:55:09-08:00","id":53525,"title":"","content":"Ok, I check it out. I really hate the Vampire Diaries though. Not my cup of tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:15:16-08:00","id":53531,"title":"","content":"I am unable to find this show of which you speak on the Wikipedia. Could you please point me in the right direction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:22:05-08:00","id":53533,"title":"","content":"I think you need to look at the CW site.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:37:33-08:00","id":53537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=53531#post53531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am unable to find this show of which you speak on the Wikipedia. Could you please point me in the right direction?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would probably be because the show is called <b><i>The Originals</i></b>, not <i>The Immortals. </i>But yes, look up <i>The Originals</i> on the CW, and you will find what you are looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:44:36-08:00","id":53541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that American Horror flick really good? It looked kinda cheesy from the trailers. </div> </div> </div>Do you mean American Horror Story? Yes, each season has been good so far, but you should know each season is a different story in a different setting. A lot of cast carry over from one season to the next, but they play new characters. So depending on your tastes, you may or may not like one particular season/story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I should give the Walking Dead a second chance. I didn't like the early episodes of the first season with the main character acting like a tool all the time. Never watched it again, but I heard it gets better with time. </div> </div> </div>I don't think it gets better with time. I think it is pretty consistent throughout. The characters develop, yes, but if you thought Rick was a tool and he turned you off to the show, don't start watching it again. You won't like him anymore in the last season, than you did in the first, imho. That said, I love the show and I have since the beginning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:32:56-08:00","id":53583,"title":"","content":"@JadedTrueBrujah<br /> I actually checked CW network and found out they make the vampire diaries, the originals, supernatural and arrow. All angsty shows with a lot (too much imo) beautiful young people. It never feels real to me. Becomes a bit like a soap. I need some old people, some ugly people or otherwise people who stand out.<br /> <br /> @Storyteller<br /> About American Horror story: Looking on youtube and trailers it seems like random scary scenes without being really scary.<br /> <br /> About the Walking Dead: I found the main character an idiot because he did stupid things in the start. Like going alone to a city full with zombies and then being surprised they want to eat him. My friends tell me they do learn and stop doing stupid shit. Don't take unnecessary risks, don't go alone in a dark cellar, double tap etc. And the focus goes from zombies to human interaction and two surviving groups competing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:44:44-08:00","id":53593,"title":"","content":"I recently found the cancelled, 666 Park Avenue on Netflix, and although I'm not yet fully through it, I think it's an excellent representation of what a Nephandi could be and do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/399-disthanes","name":"disthanes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T18:16:30-08:00","id":53608,"title":"","content":"Yeah Rick's a bit of a dope but fortunately everyone else isn't. Well for the most part, there are some other dumb people on the show but none are as prominent as Rick.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately there is Season 2, a season of long tedious boredom punctuated with sudden and often brief moments of stuff actually happening. But after that Season 3 was fairly solid and Season 4 has been really good so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T18:28:50-08:00","id":53611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=53583#post53583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@JadedTrueBrujah<br /> I actually checked CW network and found out they make the vampire diaries, the originals, supernatural and arrow. All angsty shows with a lot (too much imo) beautiful young people. It never feels real to me. Becomes a bit like a soap. I need some old people, some ugly people or otherwise people who stand out.<br /> <br /> @Storyteller<br /> About American Horror story: Looking on youtube and trailers it seems like random scary scenes without being really scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each season definitely has its scary moments, but horror is about more than just the 'scares.' The show does a good job of capturing all of the things that are great about horror, across the board. Season one is a story set in a haunted house, season two is a thriller in an insane asylum, and three is based around the supernatural in New Orleans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the Walking Dead: I found the main character an idiot because he did stupid things in the start. Like going alone to a city full with zombies and then being surprised they want to eat him. My friends tell me they do learn and stop doing stupid shit. Don't take unnecessary risks, don't go alone in a dark cellar, double tap etc. And the focus goes from zombies to human interaction and two surviving groups competing. </div> </div> </div>Well, they do learn, but learning how to survive the zombies is not the point of the show. The show is really more about learning how to survive with other humans when everything has changed. I mean, the zombies are there and they are important, but &quot;The Walking Dead&quot; are the survivors, not the zombies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:28:46-08:00","id":53972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=53537#post53537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would probably be because the show is called <b><i>The Originals</i></b>, not <i>The Immortals. </i>But yes, look up <i>The Originals</i> on the CW, and you will find what you are looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh. See when I was looking for it, I did come across a show called <i>The Originals</i>, but I didn't know they were the same. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:53:36-08:00","id":54037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=53972#post53972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahhh. See when I was looking for it, I did come across a show called <i>The Originals</i>, but I didn't know they were the same. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just discovered that the first TV sitcom was called <i>The Goldbergs</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T06:39:04-08:00","id":56087,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>True Detective</i>, a mini-series airing on HBO at the moment is pretty intense. Only two episodes in, and I look forward to this show more than any other during the week right now.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\">The lives of two detectives, Rust Cohle and Martin Hart, become entangled during a 17-year hunt for a serial killer in Louisiana.&quot;<br /> <br /> Matthew McConaughey and Woody Harrelson play the two detectives.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:28:43-08:00","id":56700,"title":"","content":"True Detective: Already heard from it. Looks like right up my alley.<br /> The Originals: It looks a bit like vampire (both old and new) only without ideological organisations. More focus on the individual that way. A bit like how I always played Requiem this far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T18:49:23-08:00","id":57146,"title":"","content":"Anybody watch Community? It took me a few episodes to get used to it but ever since its quickly risen to become one of my favorite shows of all time. I actually have a hard time describing, there's just so much to it. Its clever and inventive, irreverent but humble, and exceptionally quirky. I really like how it rewards loyal viewers through its self-referential humor. Its just so... gaaah! I hate how I cannot bring it into words! Go watch it!<br /> <br /> Six seasons and a movie!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T21:14:35-08:00","id":57214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=57146#post57146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody watch Community? It took me a few episodes to get used to it but ever since its quickly risen to become one of my favorite shows of all time. I actually have a hard time describing, there's just so much to it. Its clever and inventive, irreverent but humble, and exceptionally quirky. I really like how it rewards loyal viewers through its self-referential humor. Its just so... gaaah! I hate how I cannot bring it into words! Go watch it!<br /> <br /> Six seasons and a movie!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, and yes. It is my favorite show currently on TV - there has yet to be an episode I actually disliked, and I'm including season 4 in that statement. This season alone has been <i>bananas.</i><br /> <br /> For example, last night's episode involved a campus-wide game of &quot;The Floor Is Lava&quot;, dressed up in post-apocalyptic trappings, wrapped around the emotional core of one friend saying goodbye to another. It was incredible. And it's not even my favorite episode.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ...okay, that's a lie, now that I think about it. I really didn't like the episode with the Inspector Spacetime convention. Still, the show has a very good track record with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 01-25-2014, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T16:23:48-08:00","id":58389,"title":"","content":"I wish I could watch half the shows mentioned but we downgraded our Dish package for a lower rate. When HBO and Cinemax was on for one weekend, I was able to catch Cloud Atlas. Only seen one episode of Walking Dead. If I want Vampire Dairies, I read the 4 books that I got. I actually turned down a Resident Evil marathon. Mom and I just don't watch CW at all. Once in a while maybe My TV. Tonight it is between the Pro Bowl (Louis Vasquez, 65, Broncos is family) and the Grammys because Willie Nelson and other country stars are going to be on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T17:20:05-08:00","id":58409,"title":"","content":"I watched Firefly for the first time yesterday. I'd seen Serenity, and wasn't that big a fan, but never the actual show.<br /> <br /> My natural tendency when it comes to popular works is to assume they're overrated, so I was surprised by how much I liked the show. I feel like some of the cast doesn't get much to do, or many ways to distinguish themselves, but on the whole it was pretty good. (Also, kinda gives me a greater appreciation for the whole Han Solo archetype, which isn't usually my thing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T18:22:15-08:00","id":58442,"title":"","content":"Firefly is great even though Fox executives made it for only one season. There is also Roar, with Health Ledger that only ran one season. What I do is collect my favorite shows if they are one shots. Can't stand the teenage angst mess. Elisabeth subjects me to Glee (she only watches it for the music)...if I can catch it, I will watch Agents of Shield.<br /> <br /> There is a saying...beware of River...this is pertaining to little River on Firefly and River Song on Doctor Who...anyone who can kill at a drop of the hat is worth watching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:29:12-08:00","id":61186,"title":"","content":"Firefly is really good. Instant cult classic. It almost gets too much credit. Almost.<br /> <br /> Let me also second Fringe. First season is a mystery of the week show. Second and third season are really good. Fourth season is a bit meh and the fifth season is good but different. Great acting by John Noble. This show is really underappreciated.<br /> <br /> I also really like the nineties show La Femme Nikita. Very smart script writing, solid acting and always fascinating with just six main characters. I always liked the aesthetics from this show. The clinical decors, the metaphors (white room, information extracted, being canceled), the unemotional acting and the contant whispering. Some people may find it cheesy, but I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:48:04-08:00","id":62250,"title":"","content":"Hey, who else is relieved that Community is good again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:51:03-08:00","id":62256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=56087#post56087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>True Detective</i>, a mini-series airing on HBO at the moment is pretty intense. Only two episodes in, and I look forward to this show more than any other during the week right now.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\">The lives of two detectives, Rust Cohle and Martin Hart, become entangled during a 17-year hunt for a serial killer in Louisiana.&quot;<br /> <br /> Matthew McConaughey and Woody Harrelson play the two detectives.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like hearing my brother's humourous recaps of it in which he frames it as though it was a parody of Fincher movies, where Woody Harrelson needs to keep exasperatedly telling Matthew McConaughey (2) that he is not Morgan Freeman and Woody is not Brad Pitt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:09:01-08:00","id":62273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=62250#post62250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, who else is relieved that Community is good again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Harmon is streets ahead of Guarascio and Port. They Britta'd it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:02:11-08:00","id":62321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I agree with the implied premise that it was ever bad. Although there is one episode I could not finish watching; the puppet musical just didn't do it for me. Strange, considering the regard I hold for Jim Henson.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. Season 4 wouldn't be my favorite, but I never felt the show had become bad or unenjoyable, like many people I heard from. I wasn't a fan of the Inspector Spacetime convention, and the puppet episode seemed kinda lame to me (though I did like the starkness of the cold open). But for me, Britta's Sophie B. Hawkins dance and the Heroic Origins episode kinda made up for it. I would have kept watching even if Dan Harmon hadn't come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:17:46-08:00","id":62333,"title":"","content":"I think it was terrible if compared to Harmon's run. If compared to other shows on tv it was still fine. Season 4 felt forced and, like was pointed out in the first episode of this season, didn't have a good understanding of some of the characters (primarily Britta and Abed) and where they were headed. I rarely watch episodes from that season though I do often watch those from the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T07:20:31-08:00","id":63958,"title":"","content":"The other day, I was in a patient's room while a rerun of <b>Gunsmoke</b> was on. It's a cowboy show whose age I don't know, but I can tell you it's old enough that it started as a radio serial, moved to black and white television, and eventually upgraded to color. The episode I saw was about a little person riding into Dodge City looking for shelter and paying three drunken and probably inbred imbeciles to lock him in a barn and provide nonspecific care for him because that night was the night of the full moon, and the little person believed himself to be a were-elephant who would cause massive destruction if he was not provided for.<br /> <br /> I want some of the weed they were passing around the writers' room when they wrote that script.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T15:03:18-08:00","id":84870,"title":"","content":"The latest episode of Being Human US was one of the best shows I can remember. While being different from the UK show it ended up in many of the same places.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Sally (the ghost) goes back in time and prevents her own death. Then uses future knowledge to avert the major plot points of the first seasons. And it all goes horribly, wonderfully wrong. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T18:07:45-08:00","id":84966,"title":"","content":"It went horribly wrong because she keeps trying to &quot;fix&quot; things, and the universe is having fun slapping that ball down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:co