an the show actually called such, which is much more a straight up Horror story, full-stop. I'm sure Alan Moore's getting his beard in a twist, as he does over everything, but this is just too much fun and coolness to miss! <br /> <br /> And any excuse to watch Eva Green do her thing...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T03:23:16-07:00","id":228955,"title":"","content":"I&quot;m VERY picky about TV shows, i'm a creature of habit and like the shows i'm used to watching new ones bug..however i was recently convinced into watching Carnivale, and was hooked in first 10 minuets of episode one. I'm finding myself leaning on the edge of my seat anxiously waiting to see what happens next and guessing at whats going on. (I refuse to read for spoilers lol )<br /> <br /> I'm also watching random reality TV shows on amazon prime *shrugs* its mostly background noise while i surf the net so stupid shows like Pawn Stars and the oh so laughable Toddlers in tiaras(oh those poor children...) are usually on in the background.<br /> <br /> I was watching SG-1 again but I didnt feel like watching anymore(LOVE the show just not in the mood for that kind of show)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai