 it was next week, so I missed it. There's a rerun tonight I'll be DVRing, though.<br /> <br /> What about you? Did you see it or have any thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:30:37-07:00","id":292254,"title":"","content":"Whole Berserker vs Saber fight did not disappoint me.<br /> <br /> SABER GOT DUNKED<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:33:47-07:00","id":292257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=292253#post292253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was next week, so I missed it. There's a rerun tonight I'll be DVRing, though.<br /> <br /> What about you? Did you see it or have any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's available for free on NBC's website, so, yes, Arc and I watched it this morning. It was pretty good. Intriguing. I'll definitely be watching it at least a couple more times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:09:36-07:00","id":292749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=292027#post292027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to share your thoughts, if you did?</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it... I thought it was fun...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/170-lunatyk","name":"Lunatyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:35:58-08:00","id":311108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=236280#post236280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For people who like psychological thriller-horror stuff, Hannibal is highly recommended.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Hannibal</i> was, is surprisingly good. I'm not really a fan of the previous work on that IP, and watched the pilot certain I would stop after half an hour. I watched every episodes to date with a rare intensity. It's full of a rare depth, with exactly the right amount of horror shown. And the Hannibal character is extraordinary sober, frugal; just the right tone and direction and play.<br /> <br /> <i>Penny Dreadful</i> was also a good surprise, even if it's probably slightly inferior especially in the writing. I was expecting a League of Extraordinary Gentlemen made in TV series, with Eva Green naked half the time, and not at all.<br /> <br /> <i>Dracula</i> was a serious disapointment. Jonhatan Rhys Meyers did much better work early on, with <i>The Tudors</i> for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing on <a href=\"https://tousrolistes.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">French Online virtual tabletop rpg community</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3723-blacky","name":"Blacky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3723_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T07:41:06-08:00","id":311266,"title":"","content":"The Boardwalk Empire - Impressive, amazing, great active, overwhelming immersion into the setting. Can't wait to reach the final season.<br /> <br /> Vikings - Never seen any better series/movies about the northern warriors! Love it.<br /> <br /> American Horror Story - How the hell did I manage to live three years without this? Half-way through Second Season and loving it.<br /> <br /> Waiting on Game of Thrones and House of Cards - Nothing but pure genius.<br /> <br /> Curious about Hannibal, Mads Mikkelson is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T23:35:23-08:00","id":335848,"title":"","content":"Anyone else watching The Flash? So far it has not only met my expectations, but exceeded them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T20:47:25-08:00","id":337678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=335848#post335848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else watching The Flash? So far it has not only met my expectations, but exceeded them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am. I'm not as familiar with the DC mythologies as Marvel, so I'm sure I'm a few gags in there, but it's still good without knowing it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T13:08:54-08:00","id":339366,"title":"","content":"I fired up Netflix today and saw that &quot;The Wolf of Wall Street&quot; had been made available. I never saw it, but I heard a bunch of gushing about how good it was, so I figured I'd have a look.<br /> <br /> I ultimately quit watching just over 2 hours in, when Leonardo diCaprio spent some ten minutes flopping around going &quot;BLUHHHHH WUHHHH&quot; while nothing else happened. Kind of wish I'd spent my afternoon doing something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:44:23-08:00","id":339541,"title":"","content":"Just finished watching the first episode of Marvel's Agents of Shield. I love it! I kinda wasn't expecting it to be good, because there were several sources I trust who said the first season was just okay. If the rest of the season is like this episode, I don't see why anyone would be disappointed in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:06:00-08:00","id":339649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=339541#post339541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished watching the first episode of <b>Marvel's Agents of SHIELD</b>. I love it! I kinda wasn't expecting it to be good, because there were several sources I trust who said the first season was just okay. If the rest of the season is like this episode, I don't see why anyone would be disappointed in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The quality varies from episode to episode, but of course that happens for any TV series. Overall, the show is fine. I watch it and enjoy it. I do think the show suffers from comparison to the movies with their multimillion-dollar budgets, particularly the mid-season finale that just aired, but overall I recommend it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T21:10:14-08:00","id":339717,"title":"","content":"Personally, I liked the first episode well enough, but as I tried to watch more I found most of it to be pretty terrible (For the record, I just don't see what so many people see in Agent Coulson, I don't find him particularly interesting or likeable. The other dude is so boring I don't even remember the character's name. I also tend to dislike &quot;Hacking is magic&quot;, so I was already predisposed to disliking Skye. The rest of her character did not help). I have been told it improved considerably after it linked with the story of Winter Soldier but...well, there are plenty of stuff I can watch in which I don't have to go through several mediocre or worse episodes before getting to the good stuff.<br /> <br /> As far as superhero stuff go, I'm enjoying the Flash the most, followed by Constantine, then Arrow as a distant third. I'm hoping Luke Cage and Iron Fist will be good as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:02:42-08:00","id":340104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=339541#post339541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished watching the first episode of Marvel's Agents of Shield. I love it! I kinda wasn't expecting it to be good, because there were several sources I trust who said the first season was just okay. If the rest of the season is like this episode, I don't see why anyone would be disappointed in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The early episodes are small and slow and don't do very much because they're building up for the plot twist after Winter Soldier. Watching them the second time through at my S.H.I.E.L.D.T.U.B., they were much more satisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T02:23:18-08:00","id":345594,"title":"","content":"Well, just finished watching the first season of Agents of SHIELD, and I <i>loved</i> it. I guess I must be this show's target audience or something, because I have no complaints about it.<br /> <br /> If this was supposed to be the weaker season, I can't <i>wait</i> to start Season 2!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T15:42:50-08:00","id":362975,"title":"","content":"So, opinions on the first two episodes of Agent Carter? I liked it. In my opinion it was well paced and well written, the script was good and the characters had good development, with believable motivations and dialogue (well, sure there was some mumbojumbo here and there, but it is a spy story inside a superhero universe, what did you expect?).<br /> <br /> Since the seasons of this will be short, only 8 episodes, it will hopefully be able to maintain the quality.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the Daredevil netflix mini-series has a release date: 04/10/2015","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T16:16:54-08:00","id":362996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=362975#post362975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, opinions on the first two episodes of <b>Agent Carter</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div> It was pretty okay. Hayley Atwell and James D'Arcy have good chemistry, and I personally was impressed by the number of voices Ms. Atwell has at her disposal for playing other roles. She also has a pretty good control over mannerisms; when she pretends to be the health inspector, her body language is entirely different from when she's playing Agent Carter. The amount of superscience on display is a little annoying, though (crap is being invented in the 1940s that even Iron Man wouldn't stand a chance against), but my biggest disappointment is with the ham-fisted attempts at feminism, which I will not get into in further detail here. All in all, it's fine, and even if the show nosedives, I'll still probably watch it to the end just to see what other tricks Ms. Atwell pulls out of her acting bag.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T17:38:02-08:00","id":363066,"title":"","content":"I'm rewatching trailer park boys for probably the 3rd or 4th time now. show is hysterical. season 1 is the weakest and its still great but not as great as the later ones. if you like really crude humor with people with IQs around the same as an apple check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T19:23:18-08:00","id":363131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=362996#post362996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> my biggest disappointment is with the ham-fisted attempts at feminism</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, I also did not want to go into that but, though It appears it detracted less from my enjoyment than it did from yours, but it was the weakest point of the thing so far, I'd say.<br /> <br /> Still, my favorite of this current wave of superhero shows continues to be The Flash and with Daredevil apparently planned to be super-gritty, it is unlikely to unseat the fastest man alive from that position.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T13:21:21-08:00","id":366572,"title":"","content":"Banshee. What a great show, trapped on the Invisible Man of cable networks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T14:58:16-08:00","id":366671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=366572#post366572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banshee. What a great show, trapped on the Invisible Man of cable networks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banshee is bad in the best way. A lot of fun to watch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=362996#post362996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but my biggest disappointment is with the ham-fisted attempts at feminism, which I will not get into in further detail here. </div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely agree. For what it's worth, there seemed like it was going for a genre sort of deal rather than seriously exploring the idea. Not that it really excuses it, but I get why they didn't do something more serious (though I think they could've at least done something <i>better</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-11-2015, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T12:18:33-07:00","id":473211,"title":"","content":"I watched my first episode of <b>the Flash</b> yesterday. This show really pissed me off.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I never got into the show. The costume is distractingly awful to me, and that's that. Still, temptation was there, so last night I sat down to watch it (I admit I probably wouldn't have if Tuesday isn't All Tosh All The Time on Comedy Central) to whatever rerun was playing, and I was kind of blown away. It was a very dark episode that even someone like me who'd never seen it before could tell was really shaking up the status quo. Barry left his girlfriend for his old flame; Jesse L. Martin's character (I will always think of him as Ed Green) was targeted by a supervillain; the chief of police was attacked, paralyzed, and left with crippling brain damage; and in my favorite scene of the episode, one of Barry's little science buddies found out their mentor was really the Reverse Flash and the two of them had a powerful scene that gave one actor the chance to show exactly what someone looks like when trying (and failing) to maintain dignity over fear when a god is threatening to murder him looks like, and the other actor got to inject surprising depth into a fucking supervillain by showing us the regret he felt at having to kill someone he was fond of. After that, Barry losing his secret identity while trying to keep Weather Wizard from destroying the city with a tsunami felt almost token. I was really hooked.<br /> <br /> Then.<br /> <br /> Then Barry needed to run real fast to make a wind wall, and he accidentally went <i>too</i> fast and went back in time two days to before any of this happened. He didn't even know half of it, but he managed to undo it all anyway.<br /> <br /> I could not be more pissed off at this show. Maybe it's amplified by the fact that this is my first impression, but not only did they basically just pull the &quot;It was all a dream!&quot; weaksauce bullshit to completely negate everything that I'd been interested and invested in, they established that the main character <i>now has It Was All A Dream powers</i> and have immunized him from consequences to his actions forever, since he can now <b>Groundhog Day</b> everything he does until he gets it perfect. I can't trust anything that happens ever again because Barry might just run to the past and fix it.<br /> <br /> Fuck. You. Flash.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:48:14-07:00","id":473599,"title":"","content":"Flash's speed and the Speed Force are particularly awful powers. I don't like the show myself but I've been tuning in on the Captain Cold and Heatwave episodes. It was great to see Roger Howarth acting in primetime again but I was disappointed by his role and how it turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-08-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2