und: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You see time progression. The city with litter, boarded up windows. A cop drives by shining his searchlight. the camera pans up to... Damon. Standing on the ledge of a clocktower, looking down at the city. END. Then the producers come on to say &quot;Tune in this fall to see how Damon deals with life without Elena!&quot; All I could think was, &quot;Holy fuck! He's Batman!&quot;</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh! <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Looking forward to seeing if they add new characters, or pair him up with existing ones, like Bonnie.</div></div> </div> </div> Looking forward to more Originals, too (tho I wish they'd come up with a better name for it)!<br /> <br /> Flash's season ended ok; looking forward to Supergirl and Legends of Tomorrow, which look like good old-fashioned FUN. Now *that's* what's missing in super hero adaptations these days! Marvel gets it, it's about time DC did, too! Having said that, I'm hoping Lucifer picks up where Constantine left off...<br /> <br /> Penny Dreadful was awesome...right up till the end of this season. Maybe I need to rewatch it, but something felt a bit OFF about the conclusion. True Detective S2 is fairly entertaining, but meandering, doesn't really felt like it's going anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:12:59-07:00","id":612590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=532010#post532010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I'd fit the role of spoiled American. Give me a soap opera, professional wrestling and an ongoing comic and I'm content.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still miss One Life To Live; General Hospital tries, but it's just not doing it for me...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sometimes I'll put on WWE for background noise (andthe Divas!), but I haven't really paid attention to it since the good old days of Stone Cold and The Rock...<br /> <br /> Last ongoing comic I was reading was Loki, Agent of Asgard, but crossovers killed it, apparently. I did pick up the new launch of Archie, if only just to have the first issue...Mark Waid tells a very likable reboot story, so I might stick with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:48:35-07:00","id":612915,"title":"","content":"The Whispers, Mr. Robot, (Seems like good inspiration for Demon: the Descent) Extant, Dominion, Dark Matter, Defiance, Killjoys, Last Ship, Falling Skies, Zoo, Scream, Humans, Rick &amp; Morty, &amp; The Strain. Surprisingly busy Summer season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-03-2015, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:58:06-07:00","id":612927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=612590#post612590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still miss One Life To Live; General Hospital tries, but it's just not doing it for me...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree, it was nice bringing Todd over, but now he's not Todd anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sometimes I'll put on WWE for background noise (andthe Divas!), but I haven't really paid attention to it since the good old days of Stone Cold and The Rock... </div> </div> </div>There's some fun stuff there, they're doing a lot of new ideas.<br /> <br /> But really I don't watch that much tv, at least new stuff. I saw some episodes of some crime shows but they weren't worth watching any longer. Black Sails, Gotham, Inside No. 9 and House of Fools. Netflix has been nice enough to bring me Bojack Horseman, which has been consistently good so far. I'm not through the second season yet, though.<br /> <br /> Oh. Nathan For You has been fucking hilarious.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/86074e15a83ca8995594922f2226f871/tumblr_mjdczkYecS1qapglso1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:13:39-07:00","id":612939,"title":"","content":"Just binged-watched yesterday the second season of Penny Dreadful -- it had its flaws (the narrative &quot;dips&quot; become perhaps more noticeable when viewing the episodes back-to-back-to-back), and a few specific bits could have been handled better, but overall I was as happy with it as I was with the first season (and its similar flaws). The third episode, though, with Patti Lupone? -- <b><i>Fucking Amaze-Balls!!! </i></b> She was just fantastic. She and Eva Green had an instant chemistry that rarely happens in a single episode of an ongoing series (especially when one person is just a guest star who -- for built-in narrative reasons -- will almost certainly never be on the show again).<br /> <br /> While the flaws of the show can be slightly annoying (Dorian's role this season left his character feeling more two-dimensional than last season; some plot points get dropped for couple episodes or more at a time that diminishes their comparative relevance rather than strengthening them -- &quot;whetting the viewers' appetites&quot;, as it were; a couple characters get influenced in ways that are &quot;questionable&quot; relative to how on-guard they all are supposed to be given what is indicted in-story and by said characters, themselves; et al.), the tone, ambiance and the casting (*particularly* Eva Green, Josh Hartnett and Timothy Dalton, with Billie Piper giving good turn this season as her character is significantly different/changed from last season, and others) more than makes up for the short-comings. I'd recommend it for anybody who likes period-setting supernatural/horror, and particularly for anyone WoD-minded (the show is very NWoD-feeling in the context that the supernatural clearly exists, but it is more low-key/powered compared to CWoD).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:20:18-07:00","id":613931,"title":"","content":"Penny Dreadful is a show I've been wanting to try, but I can't find the first season anywhere. It's not on Netlix, it's not on demand, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T22:12:12-07:00","id":614585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=613931#post613931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny Dreadful is a show I've been wanting to try, but I can't find the first season anywhere. It's not on Netlix, it's not on demand, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your local library might have it on DVD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:37:38-07:00","id":614959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=613931#post613931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny Dreadful is a show I've been wanting to try, but I can't find the first season anywhere. It's not on Netlix, it's not on demand, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't OnDemand in your area? It (the first season) was in mine when I watched it this past Saturday -- I had even accidentally clicked on it and hit episode 3 when trying to bring up the Lupone episode, by mistake. Check again. Maybe you somehow overlooked it? (Of course, not all areas carry the exact same stuff, but I can't imagine Showtime not being &quot;universal&quot; in terms of what it has available OnDemand vs. what more basic channels may/may not be available or have OnDemand...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":". 08-04-2015, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:09:40-07:00","id":615012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=612927#post612927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to agree, it was nice bringing Todd over, but now he's not Todd anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's still entertaining, and it was really cool to see him show up on The Flash! But the OLTL actors who played Starr and John have left (replaced and killed off), so he's the only remnant left...<br /> <br /> Did you watch the online version after the show ended? I only caught a few eps, and can't find them on Youtube anymore...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> But really I don't watch that much tv, at least new stuff. I saw some episodes of some crime shows but they weren't worth watching any longer. Black Sails, Gotham, Inside No. 9 and House of Fools. Netflix has been nice enough to bring me Bojack Horseman, which has been consistently good so far. I'm not through the second season yet, though.<br /> <br /> Oh. Nathan For You has been fucking hilarious. </div> </div> </div>I like Gotham, and really need to watch more Black Sails. Loved the first season of DaVinci's Demons, need to watch the second. Black Mirror is an interesting show, tho it's more Outer Limits than Twilight Zone, whatever Netflix says. Danger Five (also on Netflix) is freaking hysterical! Can't wait for more Archer, It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia and Rick and Morty! Never heard of Nathan For You...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:16:27-07:00","id":615028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=613931#post613931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penny Dreadful is a show I've been wanting to try, but I can't find the first season anywhere. It's not on Netlix, it's not on demand, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, OnDemand has a bad habit of not having entire seasons, or of missing the first few eps of a season, as though people don't like to start at the beginning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more positive note, does anyone know when the next Binge Week is coming up? That's where OD just makes everything freely available for all cable users to watch, even without subscriptions...I just caught the tail end of the last one.<br /> <br /> And yes, PD is a great show. I'm sucked into anything Eva Green is a part of, but Billie Piper esp just wowed me in the last season! I'm starting to think she was greatly underutilized on Doctor Who...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:03:49-07:00","id":615318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=614959#post614959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't OnDemand in your area? It (the first season) was in mine when I watched it this past Saturday -- I had even accidentally clicked on it and hit episode 3 when trying to bring up the Lupone episode, by mistake. Check again. Maybe you somehow overlooked it? (Of course, not all areas carry the exact same stuff, but I can't imagine Showtime not being &quot;universal&quot; in terms of what it has available OnDemand vs. what more basic channels may/may not be available or have OnDemand...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Just checked again. It has all of season 2 On Demand, but not a single episode from season 1. Just season 1 recap video shorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:54:38-07:00","id":615414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=615318#post615318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Just checked again. It has all of season 2 On Demand, but not a single episode from season 1. Just season 1 recap video shorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, dude. Don't know what to tell you. It was on in my area this past weekend; maybe it dropped here, too, though I'd have to wait until later to check. Sorry!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:53:37-07:00","id":615481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=615414#post615414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, dude. Don't know what to tell you. It was on in my area this past weekend; maybe it dropped here, too, though I'd have to wait until later to check. Sorry!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all good. Hopefully it appears on Netflix or Amazon Prime at some point in the near future. The show seems like it'd be right up my alley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:55:52-07:00","id":615929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=615481#post615481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all good. Hopefully it appears on Netflix or Amazon Prime at some point in the near future. The show seems like it'd be right up my alley.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty much a NWoD Victorian chronicle. I started a thread about it a while back: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/568848-penny-dreadful-for-your-thoughts\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-your-thoughts</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T01:01:14-07:00","id":616076,"title":"","content":"I've just finished watching <i>Humans</i> with my little sister.<br /> It's a cool show set in a world where the technology to create androids exists and is widely utilised... and the man behind it went ahead and made some 'machines' with conciousness.<br /> Oddly enough, I quite enjoyed the background music in some of the scene interactions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/170-lunatyk","name":"Lunatyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:22:03-07:00","id":618076,"title":"","content":"I'm arriving super late to the party and watching Red vs Blue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2152-phyi","name":"Phyi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2152_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T01:14:50-07:00","id":618634,"title":"","content":"I've only ever saw the first few episodes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/170-lunatyk","name":"Lunatyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T18:08:35-07:00","id":622949,"title":"","content":"I really liked watching hemlock grove and sense8, both are netflix originals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T07:27:52-07:00","id":623280,"title":"","content":"Newish to me shows:<br /> Steven Universe: A fantastic animated series with short but deep episodes and a slowly growing mythology. Highly recommended, though the main character is a tad annoying in the first couple episodes.<br /> Another Period: A guilty pleasure. Everything I liked about Downton Abbey without any pretense of seriousness.<br /> Sex, Drugs, and Rock &amp; Roll: Denis Leary as a trashed out rock star. Need I say more?<br /> Mr. Robot: A cerebral take on the cyberpunk genre. Not sure if the main character is supposed to be autistic, brain damaged, or suffering from deep trauma. Possibly all three.<br /> Sense8: Transhumanism from JMS and the Wachowskis. Need I say more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T13:19:03-07:00","id":623613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=622949#post622949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked watching hemlock grove and sense8, both are netflix originals</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh, I thought Hemlock Grove was one of the worst shows I've seen in the last decade. Horrid acting, pacing, story, etc. Just a trainwreck of crap.<br /> <br /> I gave it three episodes to try to see what some others were seeing, but I'm not sure I could give it any more of my time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:52:59-07:00","id":631865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=623280#post623280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. Robot: A cerebral take on the cyberpunk genre. Not sure if the main character is supposed to be autistic, brain damaged, or suffering from deep trauma. Possibly all three.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's all of the above. Anyone else think this works as inspiration for Demon: the Descent? The plot revolves around a deeply troubled hacker, trying to sabotage a massive global corporation. One of the episodes has &quot;daemon&quot; in the title, which I feel fits the nature of the Unchained better than calling them Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:07:49-07:00","id":633080,"title":"","content":"I just started watching it. Originally avoided it but apparently Christian Slater's in it, which is cool, because I like him and hopefully he'll break his show-killer streak. I like the show, too, he's arguably a minor part but the main stuff is good and interesting. Sort of like Hannibal, in the direction, not the story.<br /> <br /> I followed someone else's mention of Another Period, and have found that to be great as well. Plus Christina Hendricks, woo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T21:26:41-07:00","id":667773,"title":"","content":"Tonight's episode of South Park was quite possibly my favorite episode ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T21:35:36-07:00","id":667798,"title":"","content":"It was pretty good yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:47:37-07:00","id":668082,"title":"","content":"With as many people as I've spoken with who act like they seriously believe the PC Police are a real thing running around physically assaulting people, I'm left feeling uncertain as to how ironic the episode was, which detracted from my enjoyment; but I'll credit the show's creative team with enough intelligence to not be passing along that message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:37:42-07:00","id":668291,"title":"","content":"I recently finished American Horror Story: Coven. I liked it, very Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:38:16-07:00","id":678454,"title":"","content":"A year or so ago I found a beautiful show, and I'm so pleased and eager to find that the third season is coming next month.<br /> <br /> Here's the trailer, censored but possibly NSFW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHBaVVIrONI\" data-code=\"bHBaVVIrONI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bHBaVVIrONI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I <i>think </i>all the old episodes are online on Comedy Central's site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T14:10:06-07:00","id":680387,"title":"","content":"Ok here's some of the shows I'll be watching this season:<br /> <br /> Doctor Who: I'm a Whovian, so yeah pretty much expected. I love what they've done with the Twelfth Doctor in terms of personality.<br /> <br /> Sleepy Hollow: I wasn't too much of a fan of the second half of the second season but I'm still curious to see what they'll do with the Headless Horseman.<br /> <br /> Once Upon a Time: I love this show, Robert Carlyle and Lana Parilla as Rumplestiltskin and the Evil Queen are what sell this show though I am pissed at the massive Disney incursion that occurred the last season (Note to Disney: This show does not exist to hawk your fairy tale franchises, knock it off or the mouse gets some rebar shoved where the sun don't shine.).<br /> <br /> Daredevil: Yeah I'm late to the party, but I only recently got Netflix so sue me.<br /> <br /> Grimm: I love they've done with this show and the overarching plot doesn't bug like the inane demon plot in Supernatural did probably because the show knows how to balance itself between said plot and being a monster of the week set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:57:02-07:00","id":682048,"title":"","content":"BBCA has been airing classic episodes of Tom Baker's run on Doctor Who. Generally speaking, they are painfully cheesy (late 70s BBC SFX and scriptwriting leave something to be desired), but it was nice seeing Sarah Jane as a young woman, and I'm finally meeting other Time Lords and Ladies and <i>Genesis of the Daleks</i> was a very interesting thing to watch inbetwixt the two halves of this year's season premiere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:11:47-07:00","id":682599,"title":"","content":"Old Who was indeed cheesy but that's part of its charm. That's said I tend to dislike a lot of the Fourth Doctor's tenure. Baker was on way too long and it seeped into his acting to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T21:37:45-07:00","id":682637,"title":"","content":"I've been loving Scream Queens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:13:06-07:00","id":707491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=682048#post682048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BBCA has been airing classic episodes of Tom Baker's run on Doctor Who. Generally speaking, they are painfully cheesy (late 70s BBC SFX and scriptwriting leave something to be desired), but it was nice seeing Sarah Jane as a young woman, and I'm finally meeting other Time Lords and Ladies and <i>Genesis of the Daleks</i> was a very interesting thing to watch inbetwixt the two halves of this year's season premiere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man, I hadn't seen those eps in awhile; I had a River Song moment, &quot;He's so <i>young!</i>&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Also, his performance was a lot more physical than I'd remembered, lots of running, jumping, even some fighting...<br /> <br /> Speaking of other Time Lords, did you see City of Death, featuring the most awesome Time Lady ever, Romana? The fact that the actors really fell for each other and got married really comes through in their performance, to the degree you can even say that this isthe first romantic relationship in the series between Doc and Companion! <br /> <br /> I don't know why they chose to show those eps now, but I hope they get a large enough response to them to make this a permanant feature of BBCA's schedule. They could show CDW in order, or even just random eps, switching the Docs up every week, why not? Do they really *need* to show so many eps of Top Gear or whatever?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T10:03:08-07:00","id":708891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=707491#post707491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of other Time Lords, did you see City of Death, featuring the most awesome Time Lady ever, Romana? The fact that the actors really fell for each other and got married really comes through in their performance, to the degree you can even say that this is the first romantic relationship in the series between Doc and Companion!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, City of Death is one of the ones they showed. It was fun. I even saw Logopolis, which is my only exposure to Adric, who sadly did not live up to the hype. He was not nearly as annoying as Tom-This-Is-My-Last-Episode-Lets-Get-It-Overwith-Baker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T18:14:29-07:00","id":730563,"title":"","content":"Color me surprised: I'm getting into the Arrow and Flash scene.<br /> <br /> Well, I guess I shouldn't <i>really</i> be surprised. Considering how much I like the Marvel stuff, well-done superhero media seems to officially be one of my &quot;things.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T16:01:15-07:00","id":733321,"title":"","content":"Game Show Network (GSN) is experimenting with an interesting &quot;haunted house&quot;-themed game show. <b>Hellevator</b> debuted last week, immersing the contestants in the story of a murderous undertaker. And it looks very promising, using a lot of traditional haunted house tricks to spice up each challenge. The second one, for example, was getting exactly twelve pounds of &quot;human organs&quot; on a scale. And as the contestant start removing organs from a pair of &quot;cadavers&quot;, they suddenly woke up and started screaming and begging for help. Classic gimmick, new venue. <br /> <br /> Not sure how well it will fare as we move farther away from Halloween. But for now, it looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:46:16-08:00","id":753894,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of canceling my recordings of the new Muppet Show. Uncle Deadly is the only consistently good character, and every single episode has at least one plotline that is &quot;Kermit is a terrible person and you should despise him&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T23:29:56-08:00","id":765382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5874-tv-discussion-what-are-you-watching?p=753894#post753894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of canceling my recordings of the new Muppet Show. Uncle Deadly is the only consistently good character, and every single episode has at least one plotline that is &quot;Kermit is a terrible person and you should despise him&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been reading lots of back-and-forth about this series, largely along the lines of &quot;This sucks, the Muppets that I watched growing up didn't have adult humor in it!&quot; and &quot;Oh, it *absolutely* did, you just weren't old enough to <i>notice</i> it back then!&quot; Similarly, while many don't like the unpleasant qualities of Kermit, others point out that he *always* had those qualities, although they may be admittedly more pronounced now. OTOH, Kermit in the movies was more of an all-around Nice Guy, and that's probably had more impact on the collective memory of the character. <br /> <br /> So, in a way, the new show is just getting Back To Basics. <br /> <br /> For a similar approach to another children's icon, look at Bugs Bunny's new show &quot;Wabbit.&quot;, which gives all the folks who complained about The Looney Toons Show what they wanted. Personally, I thought TLTS was *fantastic*, and can barely watch the new one. It's not *bad*, it's just...the Looney Toons have Been There and Done That, and this isn't really an improvement. In fact, TLTS specifically avoided that type of show <i>because</i> it had already been done and they knew they couldn't top the original LT shorts, and they wanted to go in a new direction with these characters! <br /> <br /> I really hope the people whose complaints brought about Wabbit. watch it and realize, &quot;Oooh, yeah...<b>Now</b> I get why they didn't just do this in the first place...yeah, bring back the other show.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T23:48:11-08:00","id":765398,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I'm still watching what I laughably refer to as my &quot;guilty pleasure shows&quot;, The Vampire Diaries and The Originals. And I wonder if I'm the only one here watching the latter who raised an eyebrow on its introduction of a powerful vampire society called &quot;The Strix&quot;? I mean, it's different enough from Requiems' Strix, being more like the Camarilla or the Invictus, but still, what are the odds? Hope WW isn't still in the mood to sue other vamp franchises these days...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Post